mode: "100644"
text: "# Scope, distinctions & connections\n\n## Honest scope (never violate)\n- **The agent** runs the fit test, writes the spoken-word script (locked before render), plans scenes/brand\n  kit/localization + the QA gates, and — **where the API is connected** (Creator+ tier) — can drive generation\n  programmatically. Where it isn't, exact steps for the human in-app. No pretended automation; **no unreviewed\n  auto-publish.**\n- **The human approves every video** — the agent can't watch a render and never fabricates \"that looks\n  natural\"; native-speaker QA per localized language.\n- **WoopSocial publishes** the finished exports (measurement: the platforms' native analytics); it does **not** generate avatars or\n  edit video. LMS/SCORM distribution is separate (Enterprise; the human's LMS).\n- **The consent spine:** stock avatars = consented paid actors; personal avatars = the owner's live consent\n  recording (single-take source, never spliced); **never** an avatar of anyone without verified consent — no\n  celebrities/politicians/competitors, no fake endorsements (impersonation prohibited by platform and stack).\n- **Disclosure, always:** a synthetic presenter is labeled (YouTube altered-content, TikTok AI tag, EU AI Act\n  synthetic-media obligations from Aug 2026, C2PA where available). **YMYL:** avatar delivery doesn't lower the\n  claim bar — health/finance content keeps sourcing + not-professional-advice framing, and regulated topics may\n  hit 12–24h moderation review (plan for it). **Never fabricate** tiers, gates, render times, or capabilities —\n  verify in-app (verify-quarterly).\n\n## Distinct from its siblings (route correctly)\n- **heygen** = the creator/social-native avatar lane (more casual TikTok feel; this = the enterprise/L&D/\n  localization lane — test both on your format; state trade-offs, don't fabricate a winner).\n- **talking-head-and-piece-to-camera** = the REAL human on camera (trust-led content routes there; the hybrid\n  split is the pro move).\n- **ai-video / luma / veo-3 / kling** = cinematic/generative footage (no presenter); Synthesia's AI Playground\n  embeds Veo 3.1 (and, until OpenAI's Sora API sunsets Sept 24 2026, Sora 2) for B-roll inside its editor.\n- **ai-voiceover / elevenlabs** = voice-only narration (no face); **descript** = editing recorded talk content\n  (its avatars/Eye Contact patch a recording; this generates the presenter).\n- **short-form-video-script / educational-content-and-how-to** = the scripts this renders.\n- **capcut** = post-render captions/pace where needed.\n\n## Where this connects\n- **Reads first:** the content skill (educational-content-and-how-to / short-form-video-script) +\n  brand-profile + voice-builder (the script's voice) + design-and-templates (brand kit).\n- **Feeds:** capcut (captions/pace), youtube-publishing-and-metadata / tiktok-video-publishing /\n  instagram-reels-publishing (the finished file), email-and-newsletter (embedded explainers),\n  lead-magnets-and-funnels (course/onboarding video).\n- **Publishes via:** export → scheduling-and-queue → **WoopSocial** (social); the LMS (training — human).\n- **Tool file:** `tools/integrations/synthesia.md` (tiers, gates, the consent architecture, API).\n- **Measure with:** native + analytics-and-reporting on completion/watch-through — never fabricated.\n"
